# Design goals

Good guardrails share these properties:

| Property | Why it matters |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Progressive** | Legacy debt does not block all forward motion |
| **Diff-aware** | Gates judge what _your change_ did, not the whole tree |
| **Layered** | Cheap automation first; expensive human judgment on what remains |
| **Documented ↔ enforced** | Every written standard maps to a check, a reviewer question, or both |
| **Agent-friendly** | Machines get explicit contracts (schemas, severity tags, output formats) |
| **Scoped fixes** | Never mass-rewrite unrelated files to get green |
| **Spec-backed** | Build contracts are testable; bugs update the contract, not just the code |

